// A workspace of one, which is a strange thing to write down until you
// see what it is for. The workspace one directory up ties the client to
// the five library modules it links against, and every module in a
// workspace shares one module graph, so putting this one in it would
// make a build of an analyzer depend on resolving five libraries that
// are not published yet.
//
// This analyzer imports nothing from the client. It reads source. So
// it stands on its own, and the only reason this file exists is that a
// workspace found by walking up would otherwise claim a directory it
// does not list.

go 1.26.6

use .
